+## Kato applicability and the Version 13 consumer
+
+The active mathematical dependency baseline for this contribution is the [Version 13 manuscript](../../../manuscripts/quartic_v13.tex), which retains the [Version 11 Kato repair](../../../manuscripts/quartic_v11.tex) unchanged. The [Version 13 carry-forward record](../../../docs/quartic-318-326/v13-consumer-binding/APPLICATION.json) binds the current construction, norm identities, limiting class and downstream passages to the previously reviewed [Version 11 application and consumer record](../../../docs/quartic-318-326/v11-consumer-binding/APPLICATION.json). The preserved [historical Version 10 pin](sources/quartic_v10.tex) is not the active smaller-index interface. This adopts the exact repaired interface at the current baseline; it does not assert a complete revalidation of the restricted converse or a completed Lean witness-existence proof.
+
+Version 12's 498/514-variable reduction and Version 13's 394/411-variable reduction are distinct from this contribution's literal 318/326 construction. Their new order-12/order-10 and order-40 tests, point-domain changes and scalar reductions are not automatically substituted for the current order-4/order-13, index-8 and height-49/8 source. The carry-forward verifies the retained arithmetic dependencies and leaves those separate new reductions and their application to this source outside its acceptance scope.
 
 The primary source is K. Kato, *Euler systems, Iwasawa theory, and Selmer groups*, Kodai Mathematical Journal 22 (1999), 313–372, [published PDF](https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/kodaimath1978/22/3/22_3_313/_pdf), DOI [10.2996/kmj/1138044090](https://doi.org/10.2996/kmj/1138044090). Its pinned PDF SHA-256 is `483dc18c56b2fe9cfac4e37f2e6594399625c3f0ea98a05bb69116377c67fc06`. Kato 2004, *p-adic Hodge theory and values of zeta functions of modular forms*, Astérisque 295, supplies the original class construction and Proposition 8.12 norm relation; the pinned PDF SHA-256 is `3c6e14b11fa60262db8aff782ce3cf4d83e9100c0be83621a7e4ce502cec605d`.
 
